 "about": "BiGym 2.0 benchmark (G1 with Dex1 grippers, its own GR00T-WBC controller, target=truth), the two tasks the seed skill covers: reach_target_single (touch the red sphere with the left hand) and drawer_top_open (open the top drawer of the kitchen cabinet). Episodes are `<task>/<pool>/<n>`: the diagnostic pool is the practice pool P (the first 10 indices of each task, 20 in all); the acceptance pool is a block of 20 consecutive indices per task of the pool A (40 in all) and the sealed pool one of 30 per task of the pool S (60 in all), both at an offset a hidden seed chooses; BiGym's evaluation seeds [620000, 630000) are no pool. One MuJoCo simulator at a time (CPU). Bench variant (TODO 49.7a): runs on the bench adapter locomani.bench.bigym2 through the generic backend (backend_bench.py); the package is the adapter's seed (skill.py, frozen __init__.py).",
